# The build's known-vulnerable-component gate and its exceptions (waivers, unknown-version allowances) are reviewed by
# the owner, not by whoever commits them: a waiver's reviewer= is free text, so this file is what makes a second person
# look at it. GitHub ENFORCES this only where branch protection (or a ruleset) on the target branch has "Require review
# from Code Owners" turned on, and only for changes that arrive as pull requests; without that it requests the owner's
# review but does not block the merge, and a direct push is not reviewed at all.
